## Christoffel Symbols of the Second Kind

### 1. Metric tensor and its inverse

With coordinates $(x^1, x^2)$ and line element

$$ds^2 = a^2 (dx^1)^2 + a^2\sin^2 x^1 (dx^2)^2,$$

the covariant metric components are

$$g_{11} = a^2,\qquad g_{22} = a^2\sin^2 x^1,\qquad g_{12}=g_{21}=0.$$

Since the metric is diagonal, the contravariant components are simply the reciprocals:

$$g^{11} = \frac{1}{a^2},\qquad g^{22} = \frac{1}{a^2\sin^2 x^1},\qquad g^{12}=g^{21}=0.$$

### 2. Derivatives of the metric

The only non-vanishing partial derivative of a metric component is

$$\partial_1 g_{22} = \frac{\partial}{\partial x^1}\bigl(a^2\sin^2 x^1\bigr) = 2a^2\sin x^1\cos x^1.$$

All others vanish:

$$\partial_1 g_{11}=0,\quad \partial_2 g_{11}=0,\quad \partial_2 g_{22}=0,\quad \partial_i g_{12}=0.$$

### 3. Formula

The Christoffel symbols of the second kind are

$$\Gamma^{k}{}_{ij} = \tfrac{1}{2}\, g^{ks}\bigl(\partial_i g_{js} + \partial_j g_{is} - \partial_s g_{ij}\bigr).$$

Because the metric is diagonal, for each $k$ only the term $s=k$ contributes.

### 4. Computation component by component

**Symbols with upper index $k=1$** (use $g^{11}=1/a^2$):

- $\Gamma^{1}{}_{11} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{11}\bigl(\partial_1 g_{11}+\partial_1 g_{11}-\partial_1 g_{11}\bigr) = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{11}\,\partial_1 g_{11} = 0.$

- $\Gamma^{1}{}_{12}=\Gamma^{1}{}_{21} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{11}\bigl(\partial_1 g_{21}+\partial_2 g_{11}-\partial_1 g_{12}\bigr) = 0.$

- $\Gamma^{1}{}_{22} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{11}\bigl(\partial_2 g_{21}+\partial_2 g_{21}-\partial_1 g_{22}\bigr) = \tfrac{1}{2}\cdot\tfrac{1}{a^2}\bigl(-2a^2\sin x^1\cos x^1\bigr) = -\sin x^1\cos x^1.$

**Symbols with upper index $k=2$** (use $g^{22}=1/(a^2\sin^2 x^1)$):

- $\Gamma^{2}{}_{11} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{22}\bigl(\partial_1 g_{12}+\partial_1 g_{12}-\partial_2 g_{11}\bigr) = 0.$

- $\Gamma^{2}{}_{12}=\Gamma^{2}{}_{21} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{22}\bigl(\partial_1 g_{22}+\partial_2 g_{12}-\partial_2 g_{12}\bigr) = \tfrac{1}{2}\cdot\tfrac{1}{a^2\sin^2 x^1}\cdot 2a^2\sin x^1\cos x^1 = \frac{\cos x^1}{\sin x^1} = \cot x^1.$

- $\Gamma^{2}{}_{22} = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{22}\bigl(\partial_2 g_{22}+\partial_2 g_{22}-\partial_2 g_{22}\bigr) = \tfrac{1}{2}g^{22}\,\partial_2 g_{22} = 0.$

### 5. Result

All Christoffel symbols of the second kind vanish except

$$\boxed{\;\Gamma^{1}{}_{22} = -\sin x^1\cos x^1,\qquad \Gamma^{2}{}_{12} = \Gamma^{2}{}_{21} = \cot x^1.\;}$$

Equivalently, writing them out in full (with $\Gamma^{k}{}_{ij}=\Gamma^{k}{}_{ji}$):

$$\Gamma^{1}{}_{11}=0,\quad \Gamma^{1}{}_{12}=\Gamma^{1}{}_{21}=0,\quad \Gamma^{1}{}_{22}=-\sin x^1\cos x^1,$$

$$\Gamma^{2}{}_{11}=0,\quad \Gamma^{2}{}_{12}=\Gamma^{2}{}_{21}=\cot x^1,\quad \Gamma^{2}{}_{22}=0.$$

### 6. Consistency check

This is the metric of a sphere of radius $a$ (with $x^1$ the colatitude and $x^2$ the longitude). The two non-zero symbols obtained above,

$$\Gamma^{1}{}_{22}=-\sin x^1\cos x^1 = -\tfrac{1}{2}\sin 2x^1,\qquad \Gamma^{2}{}_{12}=\cot x^1,$$

are exactly the standard Christoffel symbols of the round sphere of radius $a$, confirming the computation. (The constant $a$ cancels out of every symbol, as expected, since it is an overall conformal factor of the unit-sphere metric.)

